  "numerical_claim_scope": "This review checks joins and consistency of the retained reported model lists only. Independent whole-X/exact/RNE arithmetic recomputation belongs to donor_product_independent.",
  "wording_limits": [
    "The adapter was created after the runs; the prelaunch frozen fitter is unchanged, and normalization removes only four true stability annotations in memory.",
    "The old-v257 models admit 19,087 control rows and 368 observer rows. These numerical representations do not identify a unique K or event time.",
    "The neighbor-v258 exclusions apply to the reported single-row, wave-lane0 donor models in the actual saved-X domain; they do not exclude other lanes, multiple rows, or unrelated faults.",
    "All four wrong observer source waves have the same-invocation last-visible sampled return/resume boundary 0x80d4. This does not identify 0x80d4 as the corrupting instruction.",
    "Last-visible TTMP does not date the underlying trap or reveal full history; passing snapshots do not exclude earlier hidden traps, and nonmatching module PCs remain unassigned.",
    "The v513 LDS request precedes the sampled bank window, but asynchronous completion has not been dated.",
    "The explicit-trap sentinel demonstrated historical v257 lane0-to-v1/v513 copying under the installed handler. The current sampled-PC association is separate evidence.",
    "A shared cause with the original training NaNs remains unproved.",
    "Whole-stream and failure-payload certifications are joined to previously retained terminal audits. This review rehashes only both complete final raw records and the report/script identities, and performs no full-X search."
  ]
